# Test Best Practices for Pocketknife

## Critical Mocking Requirements

When writing tests for agents or services, you MUST mock these dependencies to prevent slow tests and timeouts:

### 1. Retry Utilities (CRITICAL - Prevents 30+ minute tests)

```typescript
vi.mock('../../src/utils/retry', () => {
  class MockRateLimiter {
    async acquire(): Promise<boolean> { return true; }
    async waitForToken(): Promise<void> { return; }
    getAvailableTokens(): number { return 60; }
  }
  
  class MockCircuitBreaker {
    async execute<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> { return fn(); }
    getState(): string { return 'closed'; }
    reset(): void {}
  }

  return {
    withRetry: async <T>(fn: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> => fn(),
    RateLimiter: MockRateLimiter,
    CircuitBreaker: MockCircuitBreaker,
    isDefaultRetryable: () => false
  };
});
```

### 2. Telemetry Service (Prevents async telemetry calls)

```typescript
vi.mock('../../src/utils/telemetry', () => ({
  telemetryService: {
    recordAgentExecution: vi.fn(),
    recordRateLimitHit: vi.fn(),
    setAgentState: vi.fn(),
    recordError: vi.fn(),
    recordEvent: vi.fn(),
    recordGauge: vi.fn(),
    recordHistogram: vi.fn(),
    recordCounter: vi.fn(),
    init: vi.fn(),
    shutdown: vi.fn(),
  },
}));
```

### 3. Logger (Prevents console output during tests)

```typescript
vi.mock('../../src/utils/logger', () => ({
  default: {
    info: vi.fn(),
    warn: vi.fn(),
    error: vi.fn(),
    fail: vi.fn(),
    success: vi.fn(),
    api: vi.fn(),
    found: vi.fn(),
    init: vi.fn(),
    start: vi.fn(),
    debug: vi.fn(),
    agent: vi.fn(),
    skip: vi.fn(),
    timed: vi.fn(() => ({ end: vi.fn() })),
    child: vi.fn(() => ({
      info: vi.fn(),
      warn: vi.fn(),
      error: vi.fn(),
      fail: vi.fn(),
      success: vi.fn(),
      debug: vi.fn(),
      agent: vi.fn(),
    })),
    ICONS: {},
  },
}));
```

### 4. ConfigService (Must return valid timeout values)

```typescript
vi.mock('../../src/services/core/configService', () => ({
  configService: {
    get: (key: string, defaultValue: any) => {
      // CRITICAL: Return actual numbers for timeout-related keys
      if (key.includes('timeout')) return defaultValue || 5000;
      if (key.includes('rateLimit')) return defaultValue || 30;
      return defaultValue ?? 10;
    }
  }
}));
```

### 5. Database Service (Use vi.hoisted for Prisma mocks)

```typescript
// Use vi.hoisted to ensure mocks are available before vi.mock factories run
const { mockPrisma } = vi.hoisted(() => ({
  mockPrisma: {
    // Define your model mocks here
    task: {
      findMany: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue([]),
      findUnique: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(null),
      create: vi.fn().mockImplementation((args: any) => ({
        id: 'mock-id',
        ...args.data
      })),
      update: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({}),
      delete: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({})
    },
    agentActivity: {
      create: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({})
    }
  }
}));

vi.mock('../../src/services/core/databaseService', () => ({
  getPrisma: vi.fn(() => mockPrisma),
  databaseService: {
    logActivity: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({})
  }
}));
```

## Test File Structure Template

```typescript
/**
 * [AgentName] Tests
 * 
 * Tests for the [AgentName] that handles [description].
 */

import { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach, afterEach } from 'vitest';

// 1. Use vi.hoisted for Prisma and service mocks
const { mockPrisma, mockService } = vi.hoisted(() => ({
  mockPrisma: { /* ... */ },
  mockService: { /* ... */ }
}));

// 2. Mock retry utilities (CRITICAL)
vi.mock('../../src/utils/retry', () => { /* ... */ });

// 3. Mock telemetry
vi.mock('../../src/utils/telemetry', () => { /* ... */ });

// 4. Mock logger
vi.mock('../../src/utils/logger', () => { /* ... */ });

// 5. Mock configService with proper timeout values
vi.mock('../../src/services/core/configService', () => { /* ... */ });

// 6. Mock databaseService
vi.mock('../../src/services/core/databaseService', () => { /* ... */ });

// 7. Mock agent-specific services
vi.mock('../../src/services/[feature]', () => { /* ... */ });

// 8. Static import AFTER all mocks are set up
import { AgentName } from '../../src/agents/AgentName';

describe('AgentName', () => {
  let agent: AgentName;

  beforeEach(() => {
    vi.clearAllMocks();
    agent = new AgentName();
  });

  afterEach(() => {
    vi.restoreAllMocks();
  });

  // Tests...
});
```

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

### ❌ DON'T use vi.fn().mockImplementation() for class constructors

```typescript
// BAD - Doesn't work with class instantiation
vi.mock('../../src/utils/retry', () => ({
  RateLimiter: vi.fn().mockImplementation(() => ({
    acquire: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(true)
  }))
}));
```

### ✅ DO use mock classes

```typescript
// GOOD - Works with `new RateLimiter()`
vi.mock('../../src/utils/retry', () => {
  class MockRateLimiter {
    async acquire() { return true; }
  }
  return { RateLimiter: MockRateLimiter };
});
```

### ❌ DON'T use async mock functions inside vi.hoisted

```typescript
// BAD - vi.fn() inside hoisted can behave unexpectedly
const { mockService } = vi.hoisted(() => ({
  mockService: {
    search: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue([])  // May not work
  }
}));
```

### ✅ DO use plain async functions for service mocks

```typescript
// GOOD - Use in vi.mock() directly
vi.mock('../../src/services/myService', () => ({
  myService: {
    search: async () => [],  // Plain async function
    getById: async (id: string) => ({ id })
  }
}));
```

### ❌ DON'T use dynamic imports in tests

```typescript
// BAD - Slow, causes module re-loading
it('should work', async () => {
  const { MyAgent } = await import('../../src/agents/MyAgent');
  const agent = new MyAgent();
  // ...
});
```

### ✅ DO use static imports after mocks

```typescript
// GOOD - Fast, mocks are applied
import { MyAgent } from '../../src/agents/MyAgent';

describe('MyAgent', () => {
  let agent: MyAgent;
  
  beforeEach(() => {
    agent = new MyAgent();
  });
});
```

## Performance Benchmarks

| Status | Execution Time | Description |
|:------:|:--------------:|:------------|
| ✅ | < 500ms | Excellent - All mocks properly configured |
| ⚠️ | 500ms - 5s | Needs review - Some mocks may be missing |
| ❌ | > 5s | Critical - Missing retry/circuit breaker mocks |
| 🚫 | > 60s | Broken - Tests will timeout |

## Checklist Before Committing Tests

- [ ] All retry utilities mocked (RateLimiter, CircuitBreaker, withRetry)
- [ ] Telemetry service mocked
- [ ] Logger mocked
- [ ] ConfigService returns valid numeric values for timeouts
- [ ] DatabaseService mocked with vi.hoisted for Prisma
- [ ] Static imports used (not dynamic imports)
- [ ] Tests run in < 500ms
